
`cop` is a cli agent written in C.

## Build

### 1. Install system dependencies

```bash
# Debian / Ubuntu
apt install libcurl4-openssl-dev

# Arch
pacman -S curl
```

### 2. Build

```bash
mkdir build && cd build
cmake .. && make -j$(nproc)
```

### 3. Configure models

Create `~/.cop/models.json` with your API endpoint and models:

```json
{
  "providers": {
    "name": {
      "baseUrl": "https://api.deepseek.com/beta",
      "apiKey": "YOUR_API_KEY",
      "models": [
        {
          "id": "deepseek-v4-pro",
          "contextWindow": 1000000
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}

```

### 4. Run

```bash
./cop                        # interactive REPL
./cop --yolo                 # skip confirmation prompts
```

## Structure

```
User Input → REPL (isocline)
     → LLM Runtime (agent loop)
         → OpenAI Stream Client (libmill + curl)
             → SSE Parser (incremental JSON)
                 → Markdown Renderer (ANSI output)
                     → Terminal
```

The agent loop handles tool calls: read/write/edit/shell

### Files
```
cop.c                    — main entry point, REPL, signal handling
cop_ui.c/.h              — terminal UI, tab completion, output formatting
agent_loop.c/.h          — agent loop: tool call dispatch & response handling
llm_runtime.c/.h         — high-level LLM orchestration
llm_parser.c/.h          — response parsing (SSE → structured content)
openai_stream_client.c   — async streaming HTTP client (libmill)
openai_sse_parser.c      — incremental SSE/JSON parser
stream_md_renderer.c     — streaming Markdown → ANSI renderer
tool_functions.c/.h      — tool implementations (read/write/shell/edit)
tool_call_parser.c/.h    — tool-call JSON schema parsing
history_db.c/.h          — SQLite session/message storage
models_config.c/.h       — ~/.cop/models.json parser
scroll_viewport.c/.h     — terminal scroll/viewport management
diff.c/.h                — unified diff generation
utils_utf8.c/.h          — UTF-8 sanitization and validation
libmill/                 — coroutine library (source-amalgamated)
cjson/                   — JSON parser (source-amalgamated)
sds/                     — safe dynamic strings
md4c/                    — Markdown parser (source-amalgamated)
isocline/                — line editor (source-amalgamated)
sqlite/                  — SQLite3 amalgamation
```

